# Intentionally empty.
#
# Wrangler merges .dev.vars on top of configured vars for any local/dev-mode
# run -- including the test suite, since @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers runs
# on Wrangler's dev machinery under the hood, regardless of the `environment:
# 'test'` it's targeting. That means whatever's in .dev.vars (personal, git-
# ignored, meant for `wrangler dev`) silently overrides the fake secrets
# wrangler.toml's [env.test.vars] deliberately provides for the test suite,
# making test results depend on what happens to be in a given developer's
# local .dev.vars file.
#
# When a `.dev.vars.<environment>` file exists, Wrangler uses it INSTEAD of
# .dev.vars for that environment, rather than merging the two. This file
# being present (even empty) is what keeps the test run hermetic: it blocks
# .dev.vars from being consulted at all when environment='test', leaving
# wrangler.toml's [env.test.vars] as the sole, committed source of truth.
#
# Do not add real or personal values here. If a future task needs a fake
# value in the test environment, add it to wrangler.toml's [env.test.vars]
# instead, not here.
